==Evolution==
Evolves into '''The Black Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''The Grey Fox''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''The Spectral Cat''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Regardless of her forms, her range and stats lend herself to generalist usage, though she is still not all that great at being a generalist backliner. You can take advantage of her long range and use her against tanky ranged enemies like [[Le'boin]], [[Le'noir]], [[Le'Solar]] and [[THE SLOTH]] to chip away damage.

If you manage to get this cat early on, use her in [[Into the Future]], as all of her forms give you a wide variety of [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|abilities against Aliens]]. Additionally, she outranges both [[Corrupted Valkyrie]] and [[Raging Bahamut Cat|Raging Bahamut]]. Her anti-Alien abilities can continue to be useful in [[Cats of the Cosmos]].

==='''Normal Form'''===
The White Rabbit is effective in stalling armies of Red and Alien enemies, allowing your other cat units to slowly finish them off. It is best not to rely on her if the target is fast and short ranged, like [[Shy Boy]] or ([[Nimoy Bore|Nimoy]]) [[Bore]], as other stallers ([[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]], [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] etc.) tend to offer better crowd control; rather, White Rabbit shines as support for such units or against messier situations, like a stage such as [[Berserk (Insane)|Berserk]] and [[Unjust War (Deadly)|Unjust War]], or stages with a variety of Aliens. Her good health and many knockbacks will allow her to stand around long enough to make a difference. In endgame, this form falls a bit behind due to her low uptime, which tends not to be enough in truly difficult stages.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
The Black Cat can be used to deal decent damage to Aliens and Reds. Use of this form is not highly recommended as her initial DPS is low, but her range and resilience may result in a satisfying performance against certain medium-good ranged foes, namely Corrupted Valkyrie. Note that this form still faces competition from her own first form, whose slow has a tendency to be preferable more often than not.

==='''True Form'''===
The Grey Fox can be used in a similar manner to her Normal Form, in being able to control hordes of Alien or Red enemies who can't be controlled too well. The abilities allow her to push everything back, regaining precious terrain in stages where slow tug of war-like battles happen, all while weakening the initial "charge-back" of the knocked back enemies. Ideal situations in which to use this feature are rare, plus such a unit only really works in armies with lots of disposable units at the core. She synergizes badly with most other Ubers.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
With her range and stats at level 60, The Spectral Cat becomes a solid generalist attacker, even more solid when against Red and Alien enemies. However, her multi-hit LD attacks and somewhat slow attack rate can put a hamper on her DPS, especially when her attacks are split into multiple ranges and only overlap in 385-466 range.

Regardless, even enemies taking a single attack will be slowed and weakened for almost 5 seconds, which is impressive crowd-controlling on top of her solid performance for her range. In addition, she gets the [[Sage Slayer]] ability, which is useful against [[Doctor K.O.]] and [[Techn-Old Hyena]], being able to prevent them from pushing as hard alongside dealing even more damage to them.

==='''Talents'''===
[[Immune to Warp]] offers a situational advantage against some [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]], making her better in presence of [[Everlord Wanwan]], [[Gardeneel Bros.]] or [[Project A]]. Due to her not needing much damage for a knockback, however, it'll rarely come into play. Similarly, [[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]] can be useful in stages that combine [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] with Red/Alien enemies, as well as those stages featuring the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]]. However, these stages are rather sparse and her range lets her avoid many Relics anyway.

Cost Down, HP Buff and Attack Buff are basic general improvements, the benefits of which should be clear. It is worth noting that Gray Fox is not exactly a combat unit though, making it so the NP is often better spent on other units. These talents do little to fix her problems, but they may be worth sparing a thought for if you are lacking units with such good range.

